cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use axonmesh in your work, please cite it as below.
title: "axonmesh: an inference decision runtime for edge-cloud AI"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "D'Antonio"
    given-names: Luigi
repository-code: https://github.com/dantonioluigi/axonmesh
url: https://github.com/dantonioluigi/axonmesh
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-07-24"
keywords:
  - edge-ai
  - edge-computing
  - split-computing
  - inference
  - object-detection
  - kubernetes
abstract: >-
  axonmesh decides whether a camera frame should cross the wire at all,
  pricing every configuration in bytes and accuracy against the same
  baselines before it is deployed. It includes the measured negative
  result that compressing intermediate features loses to sending the
  coded frame at YOLO cuts, and the measured positive one: an edge-first
  cascade that answers confident frames on the device retains 98% of the
  cloud model's accuracy at half the bandwidth, with its routing
  threshold chosen from unlabelled footage.
